🚽 Test case: a STDROT_ANY parameter (slorp's) must reject a struct
🚽 identifier, not just a pointer. ast_expr_to_stdrot_value() has no
🚽 representation for VAR_STRUCT -- without this check it would silently
🚽 fall through to STDROT_NONE instead of being rejected statically.
gang Foo {
    rizz x;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Foo f = { 42 };
    slorp(f);
    bussin 0;
}
